;; world/rooms/glasswood/x-3y5.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (-3 5)
  title: "Blue Hall"
  intent: "a hall of blue ice under the wood, where the moths come to you and light the walls: the first cave they fill"
  bed: (wind 0.05 water 0.6 chimes 0.15 drone 0.7)
  light: 0.33
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "######          ## ######"
   "####            ##   ####"
   "###             ##    ###"
   "##              ##     ##"
   "##              ##     ##"
   "##         ###           "
   "           ###           "
   "           ###           "
   "#########################"
   "#########################")
  things: ((lantern-moth at: (12 3) count: 8 drawn: 3)
           (icicle at: (16 6)))
  moment: (tune: blue-hall when: first-visit)
  decor: auto)
;; The first cave the moths fill: a tall hall with one pillar of blue ice
;; in the middle. In from the Glass Chute (rows 7-8), on east to the
;; Meltwater (rows 6-8). Its moment, blue-hall (first visit), is the moths
;; and the ice: the moths gather in H3's partials as the light spreads.
;; A spur of blue ice hangs from the roof (columns 16-17, rows 1-5) with an
;; icicle under it (16,6), over the way on east: in the dark it shows only
;; when the moth light reaches it, so listen for its ring.
